{
  "title": "CW-78",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Roland CR-78, from",
        "the service notes.",
        "14 voices, all",
        "circuit models,",
        "no samples.",
        "",
        "Every voice is held",
        "to Roland's own",
        "factory alignment",
        "table - page 30 of",
        "the 1979 notes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Playing",
      "lines": [
        "Pads (left 4x4):",
        " r1: BD SD RS HH",
        " r2: CY MA CL HB",
        " r3: LB LC CB TB",
        " r4: GU MB MAIN FX",
        "",
        "Pad 15 opens Main.",
        "Pad 16 alternates",
        "Reverb / Delay.",
        "Neither one sounds.",
        "",
        "Shift+Pad selects",
        "silently. Mute+Pad",
        "mutes that drum."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pages",
      "lines": [
        "Jog cycles pages.",
        "Shift+Jog jumps",
        "sections. Jog click",
        "opens the list.",
        "",
        "Press jog on Main",
        "to lock it - pads",
        "still play but the",
        "page stops",
        "following them.",
        "",
        "Shift shows values.",
        "Mute+knob resets a",
        "pot to its factory",
        "default."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Voices",
      "lines": [
        "BD LB HB LC are one",
        "circuit four times:",
        "a bridged-T in a",
        "feedback loop.",
        "Decay is LOOP GAIN,",
        "not an envelope.",
        "",
        "RS and CL are a",
        "700mH coil struck",
        "and left to ring.",
        "Decay is Q.",
        "",
        "HH CY MA share ONE",
        "noise source, as",
        "the hardware does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Add Voice",
      "lines": [
        "GU is a scrape, not",
        "a note - Rate sets",
        "the teeth, between",
        "the hardware's own",
        "77 and 125 Hz.",
        "",
        "MB is three free-",
        "running inverter",
        "oscillators, so no",
        "two hits are alike.",
        "",
        "CB is two tones,",
        "TB a tank with",
        "jingles under it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rhythms",
      "lines": [
        "The CR-78's own",
        "presets, from pages",
        "27-28 of the",
        "service notes.",
        "",
        "17 buttons x A/B",
        "lever = Roland's",
        "34 rhythms.",
        "",
        "Mode  Off / Play",
        "A/B   variation on",
        "      single caps,",
        "      style on the",
        "      three dual",
        "      caps",
        "Style the button",
        "",
        "Plays ONLY while",
        "the transport runs;",
        "stops with it.",
        "",
        "Pad 16 shows the",
        "FX pages; CANCEL on",
        "the web panel is",
        "Mode Off."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Roster",
      "lines": [
        "A CR-78 has ONE",
        "hi-hat - no open/",
        "closed pair - and",
        "no high or mid",
        "conga: two bongos",
        "and one conga is",
        "the whole roster.",
        "",
        "Nothing was made up",
        "to fill the pads.",
        "",
        "The Choke switch on",
        "Main is a MOD - see",
        "the Mods page. The",
        "hardware chokes",
        "nothing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Mods",
      "lines": [
        "Things a CR-78",
        "does not do.",
        "",
        "DECAY RANGE on",
        "Maracas and",
        "Tambourine.",
        "",
        "The machine has ONE",
        "hi-hat, so those",
        "two are what you",
        "reach for when you",
        "want a second and",
        "third one - but",
        "their ranges were",
        "drawn tight around",
        "the factory decays.",
        "",
        "All three noise",
        "lanes now span the",
        "same ground:",
        " HH   10ms - 600ms",
        " MA    5ms - 600ms",
        " TB   13ms - 1.5s",
        "",
        "The factory values",
        "did not move. A",
        "fresh patch is",
        "still an aligned",
        "CR-78, and",
        "golden_check holds",
        "that to the bit.",
        "",
        "CHOKE GROUP, on the",
        "Main page.",
        "",
        " Off    nothing",
        " MA/TB  those two",
        "        cut each",
        "        other",
        " All3   HH MA TB are",
        "        one group",
        "",
        "Off is the default",
        "and is inert.",
        "",
        "A CR-78 chokes",
        "nothing - it has",
        "one hi-hat. This is",
        "a mod, not a fix."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Drive",
      "lines": [
        "7 characters, per",
        "voice and on the",
        "master:",
        " Diode Clip SAT",
        " BFZ PDIST Fold",
        " Crush",
        "",
        "Drive fully down is",
        "exactly dry - the",
        "stage is not in the",
        "path at all. The",
        "CR-78 had none, so",
        "a fresh patch has",
        "none."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sends",
      "lines": [
        "Rev and Dly on",
        "every voice except",
        "the bass drum,",
        "post-fader.",
        "",
        "Silent at zero, so",
        "the kit is",
        "untouched until you",
        "send it something.",
        "",
        "Delay Time is a",
        "note division and",
        "follows the host",
        "tempo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Velocity",
      "lines": [
        "Level follows",
        "velocity all the",
        "way up. 127 is the",
        "loudest the kit",
        "gets.",
        "",
        "Velocity sets how",
        "far a soft hit",
        "falls below that.",
        "At zero every hit",
        "is identical.",
        "",
        "It reaches the",
        "voices as trigger",
        "VOLTAGE and as the",
        "BA662's accent CV,",
        "which is both paths",
        "the machine has."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sequencing",
      "lines": [
        "Use Move's own",
        "sequencer: a drum",
        "track with a kit,",
        "muted (HiJack),",
        "MIDI OUT on the",
        "slot's channel.",
        "",
        "Note map: drum rack",
        "36-49 (default) or",
        "General MIDI."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
